  The reel_script and caption say the price fall is caused by the end of the Deepavali festival season, but the article attributes the drop to the end of the festival season (Ayudha Pooja, Vijayadasami, Deepavali, wedding season) generally, and the draft's slide 'விலை ஏன்' first line names only Deepavali; this is a minor narrowing but the reel_script also says 'தீபாவளி உள்ளிட்ட பண்டிகை சீசன்' which is fine — however the slides_spec second slide line '₹100' is truncated and ungrammatical (missing closing amount and the 'முதல் ₹150' range)
  The headline and reel_script single out Kulithalai as the location of the price fall, while the article describes the fall across Karur district generally (Kulithalai, Thogaimalai, Kadavur, Velayuthampalayam, Lalapettai, Vangal, Nerur, Manavasi); the draft's 'குளித்தலை' framing is not supported as the sole location
  The reel_script states the 'Kulithalai area' price fell to ₹400 for Poovan, but the article only reports ₹400 as a general figure for the district, not specifically for Kulithalai
  The slide 'எவ்வளவு குறைந்தது?' contains an unclosed <b> tag and a truncated line ('₹100' with no 'முதல் ₹150 வரை'), making the text incomplete and ungrammatical
